  "camera_score": "The film opens already airborne, a slow drift around a working orrery, and then drops flat to the drafting table for the careful work: Acts 1 to 3 are top-down, with short, crisp zooms into single terms and immediate pull-backs, like a lecturer tapping symbols on a board. The camera moves only when a symbol deserves it and otherwise holds still while the planets do the moving. Act 4 is the first release of tension: the table tilts, the sphere rises, and the camera begins to circle. Act 5 is the conductor's fermata: the camera swings to look straight down the hinge, makes its one 3x dive into alpha and holds there longer than anywhere else in the film before pulling back to watch the ring stand up through the pole. Act 6 resumes the slow orbit of the opening, now around a glass sphere instead of a star, and lets it run under the final title."
